<blockquote>
<p>I conceived it as a reaction to the preponderance of magitech things like the Scranton Reality Anchor that make it far too easy for the Foundation to contain anomalies.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I can't wrap my head around this sentiment. It's like saying &quot;I conceived it as a reaction to the preponderance of magitech things like pyrex that make it far too easy for the Foundation to contain acids.&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>(Think about how many would be completely uncontained if not for SRAs and the like.)</p>
</blockquote>
<p>And how is this a bad thing? Generally speaking, people don't usually write completely uncontainable skips because that defeats the point of a Special <strong>Containment</strong> Procedures article. Without SRAs, we'd be missing some really interesting and quality stories that are only possible because of them.</p>
<p>This article is essentially a spiteful attack on the scientific method itself. It's the skip equivalent of going &quot;checkmate, atheists!&quot;.</p>

